From: Nikita Popov <nikita.ppv@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Jun 2019 14:17:05 +0200
Subject: Fix CSR leaks in openssl

PHP 7.1 never got this change (PHP 7.2.21): openssl_csr_get_subject() and
openssl_csr_get_public_key() do not free a CSR that they parsed from a
string or a file. In openssl_csr_get_public_key() the change is adapted to
the function as it is after "Extract public key portion via PEM
roundtrip", which no longer duplicates the CSR.

(cherry picked from commit e0bafc6da440f5b028453ca19d012d6a02234fc8)
---
 ext/openssl/openssl.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ext/openssl/openssl.c b/ext/openssl/openssl.c
index c8f18bc..a55f9bc 100644
--- a/ext/openssl/openssl.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/openssl.c
@@ -3601,7 +3601,10 @@ PHP_FUNCTION(openssl_csr_get_subject)
 
 	array_init(return_value);
 	add_assoc_name_entry(return_value, NULL, subject, use_shortnames);
-	return;
+
+	if (!csr_resource) {
+		X509_REQ_free(csr);
+	}
 }
 /* }}} */
 
@@ -3646,6 +3649,11 @@ PHP_FUNCTION(openssl_csr_get_public_key)
 	tpubkey = php_openssl_extract_public_key(orig_key);
 	EVP_PKEY_free(orig_key);
 
+	if (!csr_resource) {
+		/* We need to free the original CSR if it was freshly created */
+		X509_REQ_free(csr);
+	}
+
 	if (tpubkey == NULL) {
 		php_openssl_store_errors();
 		RETURN_FALSE;
